WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.520
You know guys it seems like just yesterday the Overwatch League was first formed.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.880
But after 4 stages, 23 weeks, and 91 days, I think it’s safe to say that the first ever OWL

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:18.720
season was a smashing success! Except for the 0-40 Shanghai Dragons thing.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.460
But anyways... With the London Spitfire being your first ever champions.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:25.600
we thought it’d be the perfect time take a look back,

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.600
and give you the Top 10 Plays from OWL Season 1.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.780
Kicking off our list at number 10 is New York

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:40.860
Excelsior’s Libero, who goes on an absolute tear on Genji as he slices and dices his way

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:47.040
through not one, but 4 Seoul Dynasty players to fend off the oncoming siege.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:01:08.840
(Casting)

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:15.200
Known as one of the world’s best battle Mercys, our number nine play sees Neptuno

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:19.620
prove that Mercy can do more than just save your team’s bacon.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:24.659
With no DPS in sight, Neptuno took matters into his own hands and proceeded to wipe out

00:01:24.659 --> 00:01:30.240
three Outlaws players, all while res’ing two of his teammates just for good measure.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:02:04.480
(Casting)

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:10.560
Coming in at number 8 is the LA Gladiators’ Fissure on Kings Row, who lands an absolutely

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:17.560
disgusting 4-man earth shatter, before following it up with a triple collat firestrike to completely

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:19.400
wipe The Florida Mayhem.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:39.640
(Casting)

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:45.900
If there’s one thing to take away from our number seven play, it’s that if at first

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.800
you don’t succeed, try try again.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:53.840
With the game headed to overtime, Dallas’ OGE doesn’t let a blocked earth shatter

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:59.500
keep him down, as he recharges his ultimate in record-time to pull off one of the fastest

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:04.780
earth shatters you’ll ever see before capping it off with a 3k of his own.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:41.840
(Casting)

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:47.840
Sneaking in at number 6 is New York Excelsior’s Pine, who slips behind enemy lines to pull

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:54.500
off a series of gutsy plays to delete 4 Spitfire players with flicks so filthy you’ll have

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.960
to watch them twice to believe them.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:30.880
(Casting)

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:36.620
Jumping in at number 5 is yet another play from Fissure, who says - Who needs hitscan?

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:42.099
As he vaults through the air with primal rage to maul apart the deadly airborne duo that

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.760
known as “Pharmercy”.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:47.840
Now can we all just take a minute to appreciate this man’s determination?

00:04:48.000 --> 00:05:11.800
(Casting)

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:18.580
Number 4 on our list comes courtesy of one of the best McCree’s in the game, big boss

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:19.500
Pine.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:24.720
Facing off against the Houston Outlaws on Ilios, Pine shows off his pin-point accuracy

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:31.200
as he pops off with a ridiculous 5k that only a big boss can pull off.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:06:03.520
(Casting)

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:09.040
Coming in at number 3 on our list is Philadelphia Fusion’s Carpe who shows us that he can,

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:16.059
in fact, do it all, as he wipes out 4 members of the Boston Uprising with some crispy headshots

00:06:16.059 --> 00:06:18.560
to retake the point and win the map.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:07:00.800
(Casting)

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:06.559
Taking the runner up spot on our list, is a 2000 IQ team play for the ages.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:11.320
A team play, that will go down as one of the best to ever be seen.

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:17.200
It’s the LA Gladiators surprising everyone on day 1 of the OWL playoffs.

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:20.540
So just sit back, relax, and enjoy the show.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:54.240
(Casting)

00:07:54.560 --> 00:08:27.880
the show.

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:36.960
In the OWL’s first Grand Final, London Spitfire’s Profit shows us why he is the best damn DPS

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:38.020
in the world.

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:43.060
With 23 seconds left on the clock, Profit cuts through the Fusion’s defense like a

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:49.290
knife through butter, single handedly deleting five players to go on and eventually win the

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:51.700
inaugural season of OWL

00:08:52.080 --> 00:09:38.960
(Casting)

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:42.800
Alright guys that's our list, now if you like this video let us know in the comments.

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:45.360
And we might just give you another one.

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:46.400
"Another one."

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:49.360
Sorry that was a DJ Khaled reference, I'll stop now.

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:56.240
Thanks for watching. If you want more great content just like this, be sure to hit the subscribe button.

